{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546190408,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d349c670001qZ30h216FzG0dK","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","messageID":"msg_1d349b868001JtcF6Bjzdr95hq","type":"tool","id":"call_3de663019b9249d58f022efc","tool":"grep","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"pattern":"embed","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md"},"output":"Found 9 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md:\n  Line 75: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n\n  Line 80: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n\n  Line 89: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes, about 262 MB |\n\n  Line 93: | Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n\n  Line 94: | Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n\n  Line 133: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n\n  Line 146: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n\n  Line 149: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n\n  Line 356: | `semantic_lane_off` in a recommendation's `warnings` | The advisor answered on phrases alone. The reason after the colon names why, such as `prompt_embedding_unreachable` when Ollama is not answering or `prompt_embedding_model_missing` when the model is not loaded | Run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from the project. If the warning stays, restart the advisor daemon, which resolves its embedder at startup |\n","title":"grep","metadata":{"metadata":{"matches":9,"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Found 9 matches\n/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md:\n  Line 75: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n\n  Line 80: /doctor:skill-advisor embedder\n\n  Line 89: | Disk for `nomic-embed-text:v1.5` | 274302450 bytes, about 262 MB |\n\n  Line 93: | Warm embedding latency | 4.8 ms median and 8.9 ms p95 over 30 calls |\n\n  Line 94: | Cold embedding latency | 538.53 ms for the first call |\n\n  Line 133: 4. **Instruction file:** `embed` adds the shipped sections to your project's own `AGENTS.md`. `link` points `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md` and `REPO RULES.md` at the checkout's copies.\n\n  Line 146: | 2 | `/doctor:agents-md embed --root <dir>` | the checkout | Adds the shipped sections to your `AGENTS.md`. Skip it if you chose `link` |\n\n  Line 149: | 5 | `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` | your project | Sets up meaning matching for commands. It shows the cost and asks before it pulls the model or starts the server |\n\n  Line 356: | `semantic_lane_off` in a recommendation's `warnings` | The advisor answered on phrases alone. The reason after the colon names why, such as `prompt_embedding_unreachable` when Ollama is not answering or `prompt_embedding_model_missing` when the model is not loaded | Run `/doctor:skill-advisor embedder` from the project. If the warning stays, restart the advisor daemon, which resolves its embedder at startup |\n"}],"providerCall":{"exe