pository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"pattern\":\"Check the Install|Codex\"}"},"time":{"start":1794546205668,"end":1794546206252}}}}
