{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546209998,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d34a14b8001TkZ1cEFgZ27msr","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","messageID":"msg_1d34a0d08001aUC6aOM78ixt02","type":"tool","id":"call_80c8616d2ae94c5480e5d6c6","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md","limit":30,"offset":50},"output":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 50-79\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: To see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n72: \n73: ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n74: \n75: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n76: \n77: Run the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n78: \n79: ```\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":true},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md, lines 50-79\n50: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime install\n51: npm --prefix .skilled/skills/system-skill-advisor/runtime run build\n52: node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs list-tools --format json\n53: ```\n54: \n55: ### Check the Install\n56: \n57: Open the repository in any of the seven runtimes: OpenCode, Claude Code, Codex, Cursor, Devin, Pi or DeepSeek Harness (DSH). Then run:\n58: \n59: ```\n60: /doctor:setup\n61: ```\n62: \n63: It checks the install without changing anything. It names one repair command for each failure.\n64: \n65: Codex, Cursor, Pi and DSH spell commands with a hyphen, as in `/doctor-setup`. Devin reaches the spec-kit workflows through its `/system-spec-kit` skill.\n66: \n67: DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n68: \n69: Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n70: \n71: To see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n72: \n73: ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n74: \n75: Until a local embedder model runs, the advisor matches a typed request to a command by phrase alone. With the model loaded, a command can also match by meaning, even when your request uses none of its words. The model is `nomic-embed-text:v1.5`, served by Ollama on your machine, and the advisor calls it once per recommendation.\n76: \n77: Run the setup from the repository you are setting up:\n78: \n79: ```\n[Output truncated. Continue reading with offset: 80]"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\",\"limit\":30,\"offset\":50}"},"time":{"start":1794546209976,"end":1794546209998}}}}
