{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1794546227923,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","part":{"partID":"prt_1d34a5909001PUFObWcU3NJ8Xf","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","messageID":"msg_1d34a4f79001X0ozJgv7q3saSs","type":"tool","id":"call_df9aee72fb994a02849bac62","tool":"edit","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"newString":"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n\n`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\n","oldString":"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md"},"output":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)","title":"edit","metadata":{"metadata":{"files":[{"file":"INSTALL-SKILLED.md","patch":"Index: INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n===================================================================\n--- INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n+++ INSTALL-SKILLED.md\n@@ -67,8 +67,10 @@\n DSH loads the repository's guards and the skill advisor only from the patches a run names, so start it with `--patch .dsh/patches/guards.patch.yml`.\n \n Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\n \n+`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\n+\n To see the advisor answer a prompt, run `node .skilled/bin/skill-advisor.cjs advisor_recommend --json '{\"prompt\":\"create a readme for the utils folder\"}' --format json | jq -r '.data.recommendations[0].skillId'`, which prints one skill id such as `sk-doc`, and when it prints nothing or `null`, run `/doctor:skill-advisor rebuild`.\n \n ### Meaning Matching for Commands\n \n","status":"modified","additions":2,"deletions":0}],"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Edited INSTALL-SKILLED.md (1 replacement)"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"newString\":\"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\\n\\n`/doctor:setup` also reports a delivery leg, which reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a runtime's prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\\n\",\"oldString\":\"Codex runs a project hook only after you approve it, so open `/hooks` in a Codex session at the repository root and approve each entry it lists. Codex keeps each approval as a `trusted_hash` in `~/.codex/config.toml`, so a changed entry needs approving again, and `/doctor:runtime-mirrors` prints `PASS codex-hooks-approved` once the advisor's entry is approved.\\n\",\"path\":\"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/352-command-surfacing-research/INSTALL-SKILLED.md\"}"},"time":{