{"type":"text","timestamp":1794546250694,"sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","part":{"id":"prt_1d34aa781001Cqo3OQ0QQ26Hrz","sessionID":"ses_e2cb7b3d5ffeOOZ1uunf8eAcfG","messageID":"msg_1d34aa1060017Vm6j83bLjbv92","type":"text","text":"T019 is done and its Verify command passes.\n\n**Files written**\n- `INSTALL-SKILLED.md` (only file touched, three edits)\n\n**Verify output** (`rg -c \"@AGENTS.md\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md` then `rg -c \"delivery leg\" INSTALL-SKILLED.md`):\n```\n--- @AGENTS.md ---\n1\n--- delivery leg ---\n1\n```\nBoth conditions hold: `@AGENTS.md` prints at least 1, `delivery leg` prints exactly 1.\n\n**What changed**\n1. Section 3, Step 1 item 4: the `embed` sentence now reads that `embed` adds the shipped sections to the project's own `AGENTS.md` and leaves a one-line `CLAUDE.md` reading `@AGENTS.md`, because Claude Code reads only `CLAUDE.md`.\n2. Section 3, Step 2 table row 2: appended ` and leaves the CLAUDE.md pointer` before the skip note.\n3. `### Check the Install`: added the one sentence after the Codex approval paragraph, stating `/doctor:setup` reports a delivery leg that reads DEGRADED with the repair step when a prompt hook is missing or Codex has not approved it.\n\n**Status and receipts**\n- `git -c core.fsmonitor=false diff -- INSTALL-SKILLED.md` shows exactly those three hunks, nothing else. `git status --short -- INSTALL-SKILLED.md` reports ` M INSTALL-SKILLED.md`.\n- I re-read section 3 before editing, as the task required. I did not tick the T019 checkbox.\n- The file is dirty and uncommitted. Nothing was staged, committed, pushed or sent.\n- Skill routing resolved `sk-doc`, which returned `defer` for a targeted sentence edit in an existing guide, so I applied the doc-voice rules directly. No other file was read for writing or modified.\n\nKnown residual risk: none known. Only the two named checks were run, which is what the task asks for.\n\nNothing is blocked on you.","time":{"start":1794546247553,"end":1794546250694}}}
